    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Retire and relax at Knightsbridge, a secure gated later living neighbourhood, where independence and community combine to make for a pleasurely and leisurely lifestyle. No 12 is presented in turnkey condition, virtually like a showhouse, and so will appeal to those seeking an easy but wholesome way of life.\n\nIt is with excitement and delight that Quillsen present to the market this wonderful spacious two bedroom ground floor apartment located in this fantastic gated development within walking distance of the heritage town of Trim. This neighbourhood is aimed at those aged fifty-five years young or greater, and those younger having additional care needs.\n\nAccommodation briefly comprises; entrance hall, large open-plan kitchen/living/dining room, 2 bedrooms (master ensuite) and shower room and outside patio area.\n\nViewing vital and requests welcomed.\n\nLOCATION\n\n• Knightsbridge Village \nFirst established in 2008, Knightsbridge Village is a modern purpose-built retirement village, providing both independent living and 24-hour nursing care, along with Primary Care Services. The independent living element comprises some 41 apartments and 28 bungalows. Adjacent lie the Nursing Home, Primary Care Centre / GPs and Pharmacy. Situated on the Longwood Road on Trim`s southside, Knightsbridge Village is convenient to Trim town centre. By way of example, lying some 750 metres away from the towns Cusack-owned Castle Arch Hotel. Over the past 18 years or so, the Knightsbridge independent living units have proven highly popular with residents who wish to be part of a safe and caring neighbourhood, convenient to Trim and all it has to offer. Other facilities locally include Trim Family Resource Centre, Trim Adult Learning Programme (ALPS), Trim Active Retirement Group and Trim Men`s Shed, amongst others.\n\n• Trim\nHome to Ireland`s oldest bridge, in operation since 1393, the heritage town of Trim, needs little introduction. Set along the River Boyne and steeped in history, Trim is a picture-perfect town located 28 miles north-west of Dublin. Trim Castle, a most majestic sight in the centre of this pretty town, is the largest existing Norman Castle in Europe. One can enjoy the Slí na Sláinte walking trail which starts at the Castle on the River Boyne, routes along the Porchfields passing by the monuments at Newtown, returning along the Dublin Road and capturing magnificent sights and views of other landmarks along the way.\n\nTrim offers a vast array of shopping, with national retailers including Aldi, Lidl, SuperValu and Kilkenny Design as well as many well establish indigenous outlets; and educational facilities with excellent pre-school, primary and secondary school campuses. Trim offers an eclectic and vibrant choice of cafes, restaurants, bars, hotels and gyms.\n\nAs well as the great outdoors, Trim is big on recreation and sport with fantastic golf, soccer and GAA clubs and associated facilities, including Aura Trim Leisure Centre. It is home to County Meath Golf Club and South Meath Golf Club, as well as Knightsbrook. Others golf courses locally include Royal Tara, Summerhill, Rathcore, Killeen Castle, Black Bush and Headfort at Kells, amongst others.\n\nTattersalls and racing at Fairyhouse are within easy reach too as is Emerald (Tayto) Park, a 55-acre amusement park and zoo. Another headline Meath attraction is Causey Farm. Thrills there include Farmaphobia, Ireland`s biggest Halloween scare attraction; Christmas Experience; Summer Camp; Farm Experience; Ablefest and Dogitude.\n\nCommuting to the Capital and further afield using the M50 is both convenient and economical via the upgraded R154 (Dublin (Blackbull)/Trim Road) and an untolled portion of the M3 motorway. Bus Eireann run an excellent scheduled commuter bus service to Dublin City Centre and other destinations. Add to that, there are various bus services including a Local Link 189 that provides regular daily shuttle services on a Navan / Enfield (train station on Dublin / Sligo line) route as well as private bus operators offering commuter services to Maynooth University.\n\n• 4km Trim / Knightsbrook Hotel, Spa and Golf Resort\n• 15km Navan\n• 18km M3 (Junction 6/Dunshaughlin)\n• 23km M4 (Junction 8/Kilcock)\n• 29km Maynooth University Town\n• 30km Dunboyne\n• 29km Fairyhouse Racecourse\n• 35km Celbridge\n• 40km Blanchardstown Centre\n• 40km Lucan\n• 44km Castleknock\n• 49km Dublin Airport\n\nAll dimensions and distances estimated and approximated."
      },
